To create an LRU cache in Java, we can use a combination of a LinkedHashMap and a HashMap. The LinkedHashMap will keep track of the order in which the elements were accessed, while the HashMap will provide fast access to the elements based on their keys.

Here is an example implementation of an LRU cache in Java:
```
import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class LRUCache<K, V> {
    private final int capacity;
    private final Map<K, V> map = new LinkedHashMap<>();

    public LRUCache(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
    }

    public void put(K key, V value) {
        if (map.size() >= capacity) {
            // Remove the least recently used element from the map
            K leastRecentlyUsedKey = map.keySet().iterator().next();
            map.remove(leastRecentlyUsedKey);
        }

        // Add the new element to the map
        map.put(key, value);
    }

    public V get(K key) {
        return map.get(key);
    }
}
```
